course: dictionary
lesson: 3562
title: Ferret: an animal and an action
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can be a thing and also an action. A ferret is a small, long, thin, furry animal related to the weasel. «The black-footed ferret was thought extinct until a small group was found in Wyoming in 1981.» Here ferret is a noun, the name of an animal.
explain: Ferret can also be a verb, an action word. To ferret about or around is to search busily for something. Someone who ferrets about in a drawer, pulling things out and looking under them, is rummaging.
explain: The words around a word give you clues. Animals, pets and rabbits point to the noun. A person searching, with words like about, around or out, points to the verb. Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: Ferret, as a noun, means a small, long, thin, furry animal related to the weasel.
fact: Ferrets were once used to chase rabbits out of their holes.
fact: Ferret, as a verb, means to search busily for something.
fact: To ferret out something means to find it out by careful searching.
fact: In «The Wind in the Willows», the Wild Wood is full of stoats, weasels and ferrets, who attack and steal Toad Hall.
exercise: «The black-footed ferret was thought extinct until a small group was found in Wyoming in 1981.» What is a ferret in this sentence? | *A small, long, thin, furry animal | A kind of fast car | A high place on a hill | A way of searching busily
exercise: Ella ferreted about in the drawer for a pencil. What does ferreted about mean? | Threw everything away | *Searched busily | Painted the drawer | Slept deeply
exercise: Which phrase means to find something out by careful searching? | *ferret out | ferrets are pets | ferret through the rain | a ferret
test: Dad said, «The ferrets are sleeping in their hutch.» What is a ferret here? | A type of wet weather | To search busily | *A small, furry animal | A kind of rabbit hole
test: Grandma asked, «Did you ferret out the answer?» What does ferret out mean? | *To find something out by careful searching | To wash a pet | To run away from rabbits | To sleep for a long time
exam: Which meaning fits best in «Mum asked us to ferret through the cupboard for the torch»? | *To search busily | A small animal | A kind of wet weather | To shout loudly
